★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
Apache Pulsar's doc site versions by release *line* (`4.2.x`), not by exact artifact version (`4.2.5`). That mismatch is exactly why a naive `$version$` template (which works for the Maven sources-jar and the GitHub `v$version$` tag path — both of which really do contain the full patch version) would break here: substituting `4.2.5` into `/docs/$version$/` produces a URL that doesn't exist. The fix was to verify the real path first (via WebFetch) and pin a concrete URL rather than force a template that happens to look uniform with the other three fields.

This is also a good example of why the task's rule "verify rendered URLs before writing them" matters more for docs sites than for source hosting: Maven and GitHub both key URLs off the artifact/tag version directly, but project doc sites often group multiple patch releases under one docs branch — so patch-version metadata entries can't assume their docs URL scales the same way their source/test URLs do.
